\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The documentary record for the compounds this paper treats as simulants. Standing is graded by what the document does: \emph  {designated} names the compound for a stated measurement, \emph  {recorded} notes that it has been used without naming a measurement to validate it against, and \emph  {none} means no instrument was found. The measurement each compound is used for now is detection by a sensor, except in the last block, which lists two compounds the same NIOSH document names for filtration and which neither panel carries; they are shown because the rule by which the primary panel was built would have admitted them.}}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{tab:docs}{{1}{11}{}{}{}}
\newlabel{res:panels}{{}{12}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces What the comparison contains decides the answer. (a) For each agent, the distance to the nearest incumbent simulant (circles) and to the nearest candidate once the five further compounds treated as simulants in the literature are included (diamonds), as multiples of the typical nearest-neighbour separation of the merged space on the thirty-five-compound panel. A match requires a normalised distance below the dashed threshold \emph  {and} a distance smaller than that to every compound not designated a simulant, so sarin, soman and cyclosarin fail on the primary panel despite lying inside the threshold. (b) Matched agents under 1000 descriptor-resampling replicates (Supporting Information Section~\ref {S-meth:dboot}) for the incumbent three and for the eight literature-used simulants examined here; circles are means, vertical rules medians, bars the 2.5th to 97.5th percentiles across replicates. (c) On the twenty-eight-compound panel, which omits those five, the distance from each agent to its nearest incumbent simulant in each of the three spaces, normalised by the typical nearest-neighbour separation of that space; filled markers are valid matches. (d) Exact permutation null for that panel over all 680 ways of designating three of the seventeen non-agents as simulants, with the actual designation marked; the $p$ shown is the mean-difference statistic only, the other five and the adjusted values being in Supporting Information Table~\ref {S-tab:ablation}, where the Benjamini-Hochberg value over its eighteen tests is 0.163.}}{13}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:main}{{1}{13}{}{}{}}
